From: Folio <folio@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Clamp border-radius against the border box, not the padding box

CSS Backgrounds 3 5.5 scales overlapping corner radii against the border box. RmlUi scales
them against the box inside the borders, so a bordered square stops rounding at
`size / 2 - border` and keeps a flat edge on every side exactly as wide as the border. A
bordered element can therefore never be a circle, which is visible on any button-sized round
element and reads as a rendering bug.

The inner radii are derived by subtracting the edge sizes from the outer ones, so an outer
radius of half the outer box yields an inner radius of exactly half the inner box: neither set
of curves can overlap after the change.

Removable once upstream scales against the border box.

diff --git a/Source/Core/GeometryBackgroundBorder.cpp b/Source/Core/GeometryBackgroundBorder.cpp
--- a/Source/Core/GeometryBackgroundBorder.cpp
+++ b/Source/Core/GeometryBackgroundBorder.cpp
@@ -53,11 +53,17 @@
 		outer_radii = outer_radii_def;
 
 		// Scale the radii such that we have no overlapping curves.
+		//
+		// Against the border box, which is what CSS Backgrounds 3 specifies. Scaling against the box
+		// inside the borders stops a bordered square rounding past `size / 2 - border`, so it can never
+		// be a circle: it keeps a flat edge on every side exactly as wide as the border. The inner radii
+		// are derived below by subtracting the edge sizes, and an outer radius of half the outer box
+		// gives an inner radius of half the inner box, so those cannot overlap either.
 		float scale_factor = FLT_MAX;
-		scale_factor = Math::Min(scale_factor, inner_size.x / (outer_radii[TOP_LEFT] + outer_radii[TOP_RIGHT]));       // Top
-		scale_factor = Math::Min(scale_factor, inner_size.y / (outer_radii[TOP_RIGHT] + outer_radii[BOTTOM_RIGHT]));   // Right
-		scale_factor = Math::Min(scale_factor, inner_size.x / (outer_radii[BOTTOM_RIGHT] + outer_radii[BOTTOM_LEFT])); // Bottom
-		scale_factor = Math::Min(scale_factor, inner_size.y / (outer_radii[BOTTOM_LEFT] + outer_radii[TOP_LEFT]));     // Left
+		scale_factor = Math::Min(scale_factor, outer_size.x / (outer_radii[TOP_LEFT] + outer_radii[TOP_RIGHT]));       // Top
+		scale_factor = Math::Min(scale_factor, outer_size.y / (outer_radii[TOP_RIGHT] + outer_radii[BOTTOM_RIGHT]));   // Right
+		scale_factor = Math::Min(scale_factor, outer_size.x / (outer_radii[BOTTOM_RIGHT] + outer_radii[BOTTOM_LEFT])); // Bottom
+		scale_factor = Math::Min(scale_factor, outer_size.y / (outer_radii[BOTTOM_LEFT] + outer_radii[TOP_LEFT]));     // Left
 		scale_factor = Math::Min(1.0f, scale_factor);
 
 		for (float& radius : outer_radii)
